.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET_CIPHERS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get1_supported_ciphers ,
.Nm SSL_get_client_ciphers ,
.Nm SSL_get_ciphers ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get_ciphers ,
.Nm SSL_bytes_to_cipher_list ,
.Nm SSL_get_cipher_list ,
.Nm SSL_get_shared_ciphers
.Nd get list of available SSL_CIPHERs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Bd -literal
 STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) *SSL_get_ciphers(const SSL *ssl);
 STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) *SSL_CTX_get_ciphers(const SSL_CTX *ctx);
 STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) *SSL_get1_supported_ciphers(SSL *s);
 STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) *SSL_get_client_ciphers(const SSL *ssl);
 int SSL_bytes_to_cipher_list(SSL *s, const unsigned char *bytes, size_t len,
                              int isv2format, STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) **sk,
                              STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER) **scsvs);
 const char *SSL_get_cipher_list(const SSL *ssl, int priority);
 char *SSL_get_shared_ciphers(const SSL *s, char *buf, int size);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr SSL_get_ciphers 3
returns the stack of available SSL_CIPHERs for
.Sy ssl ,
sorted by preference.
If
.Sy ssl
is NULL or no ciphers are available, NULL is returned.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_CTX_get_ciphers 3
returns the stack of available SSL_CIPHERs for
.Sy ctx .
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get1_supported_ciphers 3
returns the stack of enabled SSL_CIPHERs for
.Sy ssl
as would be sent in a ClientHello (that is, sorted by preference).
The list depends on settings like the cipher list, the supported
protocol versions, the security level, and the enabled signature
algorithms.
SRP and PSK ciphers are only enabled if the appropriate callbacks or
settings have been applied.
The list of ciphers that would be sent in a ClientHello can differ from
the list of ciphers that would be acceptable when acting as a server.
For example, additional ciphers may be usable by a server if there is a
gap in the list of supported protocols, and some ciphers may not be
usable by a server if there is not a suitable certificate configured.
If
.Sy ssl
is NULL or no ciphers are available, NULL is returned.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get_client_ciphers 3
returns the stack of available SSL_CIPHERs matching the list received
from the client on
.Sy ssl .
If
.Sy ssl
is NULL, no ciphers are available, or
.Sy ssl
is not operating in server mode, NULL is returned.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_bytes_to_cipher_list 3
treats the supplied
.Sy len
octets in
.Sy bytes
as a wire-protocol cipher suite specification (in the
three-octet-per-cipher SSLv2 wire format if
.Sy isv2format
is nonzero; otherwise the two-octet SSLv3/TLS wire format), and parses
the cipher suites supported by the library into the returned stacks of
SSL_CIPHER objects sk and Signalling Cipher-Suite Values scsvs.
Unsupported cipher suites are ignored.
Returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get_cipher_list 3
returns a pointer to the name of the SSL_CIPHER listed for
.Sy ssl
with
.Sy priority .
If
.Sy ssl
is NULL, no ciphers are available, or there are less ciphers than
.Sy priority
available, NULL is returned.
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get_shared_ciphers 3
creates a colon separated and NUL terminated list of SSL_CIPHER names
that are available in both the client and the server.
.Sy buf
is the buffer that should be populated with the list of names and
.Sy size
is the size of that buffer.
A pointer to
.Sy buf
is returned on success or NULL on error.
If the supplied buffer is not large enough to contain the complete list
of names then a truncated list of names will be returned.
Note that just because a ciphersuite is available (i.e.
it is configured in the cipher list) and shared by both the client and
the server it does not mean that it is enabled (see the description of
.Xr SSL_get1_supported_ciphers 3
above).
This function will return available shared ciphersuites whether or not
they are enabled.
This is a server side function only and must only be called after the
completion of the initial handshake.
.Sh NOTES
The details of the ciphers obtained by
.Xr SSL_get_ciphers 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_get_ciphers 3
.Xr SSL_get1_supported_ciphers 3
and
.Xr SSL_get_client_ciphers 3
can be obtained using the
.Xr SSL_CIPHER_get_name 3
family of functions.
.Pp
Call
.Xr SSL_get_cipher_list 3
with
.Sy priority
starting from 0 to obtain the sorted list of available ciphers, until
NULL is returned.
.Pp
Note:
.Xr SSL_get_ciphers 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_get_ciphers 3
and
.Xr SSL_get_client_ciphers 3
return a pointer to an internal cipher stack, which will be freed later
on when the SSL or SSL_SESSION object is freed.
Therefore, the calling code
.Sy MUST NOT
free the return value itself.
.Pp
The stack returned by
.Xr SSL_get1_supported_ciphers 3
should be freed using
.Xr sk_SSL_CIPHER_free 3 .
.Pp
The stacks returned by
.Xr SSL_bytes_to_cipher_list 3
should be freed using
.Xr sk_SSL_CIPHER_free 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
See DESCRIPTION
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_cipher_list 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CIPHER_get_name 3
